 "notes": [
  "CA-6: no Republican on the ballot. Kiley is listed as incumbent with 'No party preference' (Ballotpedia text calls him 'Rep. Kevin Kiley (I)'); Richard Pan is the Democrat. Republican Michael Stansfield lost the top-two primary.",
  "senate-ID: Jim Risch (R, incumbent) is on the ballot. No Democrat: David Roth won the Democratic primary and then withdrew; independent Todd Achilles is in the race.",
  "LA-1..LA-6: November 3 is Louisiana's all-party (jungle) primary, not the general. The general (runoff) is December 12, 2026. Partisan primaries set for May 16 were canceled after Louisiana v. Callais; the 2022 map is used. LA-5 is open (Julia Letlow running for Senate); LA-6 is open (Cleo Fields retiring).",
  "FL-10: the general election was canceled; Maxwell Frost (D, incumbent) was elected unopposed and will not appear on the ballot (a write-in candidate did not make the ballot).",
  "WI-2, MA-2, MA-5, MA-7: incumbent Democrat is the only candidate on the general ballot (MA-5 had a Republican write-in in the primary only).",
  "PA-3: open seat; Dwight Evans (D) is not running. No Republican filed.",
  "MA-1: Republican primary had no candidates; Nadia Milleron is Unenrolled.",
  "AZ-3: the Republican, Jacob Parkman, is a write-in.",
  "CA-11: open seat (Pelosi not on ballot), two Democrats. CA-14 (Wahab) and CA-29 (Rivas): Ballotpedia marks them incumbents; both are listed as the current representatives. CA-40: two Republican incumbents (Calvert, Kim) against each other.",
  "governor-AK: no incumbent. Treg Taylor replaced Tom Begich (D), who advanced from the August 18 top-four primary and withdrew. Kreiss-Tomkins (D) has a Nonpartisan running mate.",
  "named: Gaylon Kent is the Libertarian in CO-2; Brandon Daugherty the Libertarian in MO-2; Jeremy Todd the Libertarian in KY-4."
 ],
